piiro01@mailserv.zdv.uni-tuebingen.de (Dave Rodriguez) writes:

>  I'm seeking to recover a game which crashed in the endgame. When I try to 
>restart I get the "there is already a game in progress under your name"
>message. I noticed that in the options help there is a checkpoint option
>which I have defined which seems to allow a recovery but I couldn't find 
>any information in the help file about how to actually do this. Anyone know?

>Thanks,

>David Rodriguez

Hi Dave,
here is what you have to do: get 'recover.c' from the nethack utility
files, compile it, look up the name of the file w/extension .0 that
was produced when your game crashed, then say 'recover -d
/your_directory your_file.0' and you should be able to start your now
saved game again. Hope the best for you - it's kind of bothering when
thhe game crashes in the endgame.
so long, Jo



